            "Returns [[1, 2], [5]] (list)"
          ],
          "explanation": "a[:] creates a shallow copy: b gets a new outer list but shares the same inner lists. a[0].append(9) mutates the shared inner list, visible via b[0]. a[1]=[5] only rebinds a's slot, leaving b[1] as [3,4].",
          "choiceExplanations": {
            "Returns [[1, 2, 9], [3, 4]] (list)": "The shallow copy shares inner lists, so append modifies b[0]. Rebinding a[1] does not affect b[1], which still holds [3,4].",
