            "Returns [[1, 2], [3, 4]] (list)": "This assumes a[:] made a deep copy, but it only copies the outer list; inner lists remain shared, so append is visible through b[0].",
            "Returns [[1, 2], [5]] (list)": "This combines a deep-copy assumption for b[0] with a shared-reference assumption for b[1]—the opposite of what actually happens."
